Actually, that darn cat did move over it on its own accord: I had 
arranged things so that they look like, in relevant part:

 |.|
 |.----
 |.f=@.
 |..---
 ----

I stayed still while waiting for the cat to walk over the ring; it 
did, with no message:

 |.|
 |.----
 |..f@.
 |..---
 ----

I have not moved *at all* between those two shots: I was pressing 
"." while watching the screen for pet movement. The second shot 
prompted a message area check, which yielded no message about moving 
"only reluctantly."

Lesson learned: Get your leashed pet to make multiple checks of a 
suspect item. Alternatively: displace your pet into a dead end, drop 
the item to be tested , and back off (keep the pet and item in view!) 
in such a way that the pet has nowhere to go but over the item.

